TEXT 64 32 Left 2 ;Low-side current sensing: shunt trade-off
TEXT 64 656 Left 2 !.tran 0 1m 0 1u
TEXT 64 704 Left 2 ;I = 12/(100+1) = 118.8 mA. VSENSE = I*RSHUNT = 118.8 mV.
TEXT 64 768 Left 2 ;1. Click Run: the running-person button at the top left.
TEXT 64 808 Left 2 ;2. On the schematic, click the wire labeled VSENSE (not the component).
TEXT 64 848 Left 2 ;3. Click the VIN wire too, to compare input and output in the same plot.
TEXT 64 888 Left 2 ;If the plot is empty, select the schematic window and click the labeled wire again.
TEXT 64 968 Left 2 ;EXPERIMENTS AND COMMON QUESTIONS
TEXT 64 1008 Left 2 ;Right-click a component to edit its value. Predict first, change one value, then Run.
TEXT 64 1048 Left 2 ;TRY: Change RSHUNT from 1 to 0.1 ohm. Sense voltage falls by 10x.
TEXT 64 1088 Left 2 ;Probe VSENSE; hover over RSHUNT and click to see current.
TEXT 64 1128 Left 2 ;FAQ: Larger shunts improve voltage signal but waste more power: P = I^2*R.
TEXT 64 1168 Left 2 ;TRY: Reduce RLOAD. Current and shunt dissipation both increase.
